reaches the **pre-plea** stage, where the circuits have divided and the Supreme Court has so far declined to resolve it\", \"class\": \"split\", \"subject\": \"Whether the Brady disclosure duty reaches the pre-plea stage\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"Brady pre-plea disclosure circuits divided\", \"Supreme Court declined to resolve pre-plea Brady\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0101\", \"file\": \"content/fair-trial-and-reliability-doctrines/Brady and Giglio.md\", \"line\": 72, \"claim_text\": \"(2019), leaving the split intact\", \"class\": \"split\", \"subject\": \"Pre-plea Brady split left intact by cert denial (Alvarez)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"Brady pre-plea split cert denied\", \"Alvarez en banc split intact certiorari denied\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0102\", \"file\": \"content/fair-trial-and-reliability-doctrines/Entrapment.md\", \"line\": 40, \"claim_text\": \"The Court reserved the possibility that \\\"some day ... [police conduct may be] so outrageous that due process principles\", \"class\": \"open-question\", \"subject\": \"Reserved outrageous-government-conduct due-process defense\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"outrageous government conduct due process reserved\", \"Russell Hampton due process defense reserved dictum\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0103\", \"file\": \"content/fair-trial-and-reliability-doctrines/Entrapment.md\", \"line\": 52, \"claim_text\": \"the two-element test produces divergence on the facts, not a split on the rule\", \"class\": \"other\", \"subject\": \"Assertion of no circuit split on the entrapment test\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"entrapment two-element test no split\", \"Jacobson predisposition divergence facts not rule\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0104\", \"file\": \"content/fair-trial-and-reliability-doctrines/Eyewitness Identification.md\", \"line\": 70, \"claim_text\": \"Circuit and state developments only; no SCOTUS\", \"class\": \"no-court-has\", \"subject\": \"No recent SCOTUS on the eyewitness-identification frontier\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"eyewitness identification no SCOTUS recent\", \"Manson reliability state high courts frontier\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0105\", \"file\": \"content/fair-trial-and-reliability-doctrines/Eyewitness Identification.md\", \"line\": 93, \"claim_text\": \"did not decide which post-attachment events require counsel\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Which post-attachment events require counsel (Rothgery reserved)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"Rothgery post-attachment critical stage counsel\", \"which events require counsel not decided\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0106\", \"file\": \"content/index.md\", \"line\": 43, \"claim_text\": \"the unsettled frontier of **pole cameras** (*[[United States v. Hay|Hay]]*), **ALPR**, and **drones** (bridged by *[[California v. Ciraolo|Ciraolo]]*/*[[Florida v. Riley|Riley]]*) — scale-dependent and split\", \"class\": \"open-question\", \"subject\": \"Unsettled digital-surveillance frontier (pole cameras, ALPR, drones)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"pole camera ALPR drone frontier split\", \"digital surveillance scale-dependent unsettled\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0107\", \"file\": \"content/index.md\", \"line\": 126, \"claim_text\": \"the unresolved **device forensic-search split**\", \"class\": \"split\", \"subject\": \"Device forensic-search circuit split at the border\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"border device forensic search split\", \"Cotterman Cano Touset device forensic split\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0108\", \"file\": \"content/legal-system-research-and-reference/Case Index.md\", \"line\": 75, \"claim_text\": \"whether that bar reaches Bivens claims brought in the same suit was left open\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Whether the FTCA judgment bar reaches Bivens claims in the same suit (Case Index)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"FTCA judgment bar Bivens same suit\", \"Brownback King judgment bar Bivens\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0109\", \"file\": \"content/legal-system-research-and-reference/Case Index.md\", \"line\": 94, \"claim_text\": \"the Supreme Court left open whether such an approach is constitutional\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Constitutionality of a knock-and-talk beyond the front door (Case Index)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"knock and talk front door only constitutional\", \"Carroll Carman left open\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0110\", \"file\": \"content/legal-system-research-and-reference/Case Index.md\", \"line\": 103, \"claim_text\": \"the Court did not decide whether geofence warrants satisfy probable cause and\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Whether geofence warrants satisfy probable cause and particularity (Case Index)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"geofence warrant probable cause particularity\", \"Chatrie did not decide geofence warrant\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0111\", \"file\": \"content/legal-system-research-and-reference/Case Index.md\", \"line\": 203, \"claim_text\": \"brief field fingerprinting on reasonable suspicion left open\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Brief field fingerprinting on reasonable suspicion (Case Index)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"field fingerprinting reasonable suspicion left open\", \"Hayes fingerprinting reserved\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0112\", \"file\": \"content/legal-system-research-and-reference/Case Index.md\", \"line\": 266, \"claim_text\": \"the Court did not decide the elements of retaliatory-arrest claims in other contexts\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Elements of retaliatory-arrest claims in other contexts (Case Index)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"retaliatory arrest elements other contexts\", \"Lozman did not decide elements\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0113\", \"file\": \"content/legal-system-research-and-reference/Case Index.md\", \"line\": 292, \"claim_text\": \"the Court did not decide the elements or constitutional source of a fabricated-evidence claim\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Elements/constitutional source of a fabricated-evidence claim (Case Index)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"fabricated evidence elements constitutional source\", \"McDonough did not decide elements source\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0114\", \"file\": \"content/legal-system-research-and-reference/Case Index.md\", \"line\": 502, \"claim_text\": \"expressly declined to decide whether the Government's years-long retention of non-responsive mirrored computer data beyond the 2003 warrant's scope violated the Fourth Amendment\", \"class\": \"not-decided\", \"subject\": \"Whether long retention of non-responsive mirrored data violates the Fourth Amendment (Case Index)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"digital over-retention non-responsive mirror data\", \"Ganias declined to decide retention\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0115\", \"file\": \"content/legal-system-research-and-reference/Case Index.md\", \"line\": 549, \"claim_text\": \"so the decision established no binding circuit rule on whether such surveillance is a search\", \"class\": \"no-court-has\", \"subject\": \"No binding circuit rule on prolonged pole-camera surveillance as a search (Case Index)\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"pole camera surveillance no binding circuit rule\", \"Moore-Bush no rule surveillance search\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0116\", \"file\": \"content/searches/Abandonment.md\", \"line\": 55, \"claim_text\": \"The Supreme Court has not decided how abandonment applies to a cellphone, and there is no recognized circuit split on the points below\", \"class\": \"no-court-has\", \"subject\": \"Whether abandonment doctrine applies to a cellphone\", \"search_terms_suggested\": [\"abandonment cellphone Supreme Court not decided\", \"abandonment phone data no circuit split\"]}\n{\"claim_id\": \"ABS-0117\", \"file\": \"content/searches/Aerial and Enhanced Surveillance.md\", \"line\": 36, \"claim_text\": \"Physical effects of the overflight, or observation of intimate detail, are reserved qu